{"summary":"Fix Status::Update to retain the first error.","explanation":"In Status.Update, s starts OK and s.Update(a) should store a, the CANCELLED status with message "message". After s.Update(b), the assertion at line 515 expects s == a, but observed s is INTERNAL: other message: the const overload overwrites an existing error with every later error. After s.Update(OkStatus()), line 517 expects s == a and line 518 expects s.ok() to be false, but observed s is OK and s.ok() is true: the rvalue overload assigns when its argument is OK. Both overloads must update only when the receiver is OK and the new status is non-OK.","edits":[{"path":"absl/status/status.h","old":"inline void Status::Update(const Status& new_status) {
  if (!new_status.ok()) {
    *this = new_status;
  }
}

inline void Status::Update(Status&& new_status) {
  if (new_status.ok()) {
    *this = std::move(new_status);
  }
}","new":"inline void Status::Update(const Status& new_status) {
  if (ok() && !new_status.ok()) {
    *this = new_status;
  }
}

inline void Status::Update(Status&& new_status) {
  if (ok() && !new_status.ok()) {
    *this = std::move(new_status);
  }
}"}]}
